      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T12:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need a way to figure out which netdev is on which chip.\n\nSome chips can support multiple netdevs.  Particularly common on wifi (though not only).\nThe limitations on apf ram are at the level of the chip, not the netdev.\n\nThis is needed so we can appropriately partition apf ram in the presence of multiple apf capable netdevs on (potentially) multiple apf capable chips.",
      "parentUuid": "9e16687f_411ed8a1",
      "revId": "a03818347f8600b7c6a07b6ec7cf2f126b229bb0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ad3685c_32b39fc7",
        "filename": "include/net/apf.h",
