    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc115db2_94478a17",
        "filename": "include/net/apf.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-20T11:13:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "0 should means unset not default, I fixed in the docs. \n\nAlso Renamed apf_id -\u003e chip_id and updated the docs. \n\nWe need seaparte command to set the id, it cannot be part of program installation as we need to know how much RAM available before we can create and install the program.\n\nDetailed sequence is here: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/google/apf/+/refs/heads/mirror-goog-main/next/apf_interpreter.h#48\n\nFor more background on why we design this field: one chip can run STA+STA or STA+NAN out of a singlepool (8K on current parts). GET_INFO gives the chip-wide used, but not *who* holds it. Before a install program can be called, this will allow user space to have track the chipset RAM use age in the global pool.\n\nFeel free to let me know if the updated code/doc still not clear.",
      "parentUuid": "6ad3685c_32b39fc7",
      "revId": "a03818347f8600b7c6a07b6ec7cf2f126b229bb0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
