      "message": "Some of the logic changed due to migrate to use ynl. Jetski summary as follows:\n\n```\nHere is the complete summary of all API and behavioral changes between old-api (PS18 hand-written) and the current YNL-migrated version (b0a8e46032d9):\n  ──────\n  ### 1. Userspace Netlink Naming (include/uapi/linux/net_apf.h)\n\n  Because YNL\u0027s strict genetlink schema forbids underscores in identifiers (^[0-9a-z-]+$), the family and C prefixes changed (while keeping the exact same numeric IDs 1..8 and 1..15):\n\n    Family name:     \"net_apf\"             -\u003e  \"net-apf\"\n    Command enum:    APF_CMD_*      (1..8) -\u003e  NET_APF_CMD_*  (1..8)\n    Attribute enum:  APF_ATTR_*    (1..15) -\u003e  NET_APF_A_*   (1..15)\n    Chip ID attr:    APF_ATTR_INFO_ID  (3) -\u003e  NET_APF_A_CHIP_ID (3)\n  ──────\n  ### 2. Userspace Netlink Wire Format (Attribute Absence Replaces -1 \u0026 u8 Bool)\n\n  YNL forbids negative numbers in checks.min (minimum: 0). Instead of passing required signed attributes with -1 sentinels, attributes are now unsigned and omitting the attribute triggers the default/sentinel behavior (core.c still passes -1 to the driver\u0027s\n  struct apf_ops):\n\n  • NET_APF_CMD_READ\n      • NET_APF_A_OFFSET (s32 → optional u32, 0..32767):\n\t  • Before: Required. Caller had to pass 0.\n\t  • After: Optional. Omitting NET_APF_A_OFFSET defaults to offset \u003d 0.\n      • NET_APF_A_DATA_LEN (s32 → optional u32, 1..32767):\n\t  • Before: Required. Caller passed -1 to read the whole RAM, or 1..32767 for a partial read (0 was rejected in core.c).\n\t  • After: Optional (0 is now rejected by YNL policy). Omitting NET_APF_A_DATA_LEN reads the whole RAM (and still requires OFFSET to be omitted or 0).\n\n  • NET_APF_CMD_WRITE\n      • NET_APF_A_OFFSET (s32 → optional u32, 0..32767):\n\t  • Before: Required. Caller passed -1 to install a new bytecode program, or 0..32767 to write raw bytes at an offset.\n\t  • After: Optional. Omitting NET_APF_A_OFFSET installs a new bytecode program (core.c passes offset \u003d -1 to ops-\u003ewrite); providing NET_APF_A_OFFSET writes at 0..32767.\n      • NET_APF_A_DATA (binary):\n\t  • Before: Empty (0-byte) payload was rejected manually in core.c.\n\t  • After: Rejected automatically by YNL policy (NLA_POLICY_MIN_LEN(1)).\n\n  • NET_APF_CMD_SET_FAST_PATH\n      • NET_APF_A_FP_VLAN_TAG (s16 → optional u16, 0..4095):\n\t  • Before: Required. Caller passed -1 to disable VLAN filtering, or 0..4095 to filter on a VLAN ID.\n\t  • After: Optional. Omitting NET_APF_A_FP_VLAN_TAG disables VLAN filtering (core.c passes vlan_tag \u003d -1 to ops-\u003efast_path).\n      • NET_APF_A_FP_ENABLE_IPV6 (u8 0..1 → NLA_FLAG):\n\t  • Before: Required u8 (0 \u003d disable, 1 \u003d enable).\n\t  • After: NLA_FLAG. Including the flag attribute enables IPv6 fast path (true); omitting it disables IPv6 fast path (false).\n\n\n  ──────\n  ### 3. Driver Capability Validation (enum apf_mode Removed)\n\n  • Before: apf_get_mode() enforced a rigid 3-mode matrix upfront (V6_1 \u003d 4 ops with the other 4 forced NULL; V6_1_FASTPATH \u003d 5 ops; V8 \u003d all 8 ops). Any other combination caused every command on the device to fail with -EOPNOTSUPP.\n  • After: Removed enum apf_mode. net_apf_pre_doit() only checks that dev-\u003enetdev_ops-\u003eapf_ops is non-NULL, and each handler checks its own function pointer (if (!ops-\u003eX) return -EOPNOTSUPP;, plus ops-\u003eget_ram_size when read omits DATA_LEN).\n  ──────\n  ### 4. Locking, Concurrency \u0026 Network Namespaces\n\n  • Global genl_mutex → Per-interface netdev_lock:\n      • Before: .parallel_ops was implicitly false, so all APF commands across the whole system were serialized on the single global genl_mutex, and apf_get_netdev() only took a refcount (dev_get_by_index / dev_put).\n      • After: YNL sets .parallel_ops \u003d true. net_apf_pre_doit() / net_apf_post_doit() take the per-device instance lock via netdev_get_by_index_lock() / netdev_unlock(). Operations on different interfaces run in parallel; operations on the same interface\n      are serialized (keeping the two-step get_ram_size() → read() atomic against enable/disable).\n  • Network Namespaces (.netnsok):\n      • Before: .netnsok was implicitly false (any call from a non-init netns returned -ENOENT).\n      • After: YNL sets .netnsok \u003d true. The family is accessible in non-init network namespaces (resolving ifindex in genl_info_net(info)), while GENL_ADMIN_PERM still requires CAP_NET_ADMIN in init_user_ns.\n      \n  ### 5. In-Kernel Driver API (include/net/apf.h) \u0026 Kconfig\n\n  • struct apf_ops: Removed u32 version;. All 8 callback signatures and their -1 sentinel parameters (s32 offset, s16 vlan_tag) are unchanged.\n  • struct apf_info: Renamed u32 apf_id; → u32 chip_id;.\n  • CONFIG_NET_APF: Changed from tristate to bool (subsys_initcall() instead of module_init/module_exit) because netdev_get_by_index_lock() is not exported to loadable modules.\n```",
